    steps: "1. Configure a supported, strong Wi-Fi security method. 2. Use strong administrative credentials and change default credentials. 3. Keep firmware updated and restrict administrative access where appropriate.",
    ans: "Any two: use supported strong Wi-Fi encryption, set strong unique administrator credentials, update firmware, and restrict administrative access.",
