    steps: "1. Separate cables make individual connection faults easier to isolate. 2. A failed device cable usually affects only that device. 3. Additional devices can be connected if the central switch has available ports and capacity.",
    ans: "Any two: easier fault isolation, a single cable failure usually affects only one device, and easier expansion when the central device has enough capacity.",
