    hint: "Compare alternative paths with the number of required connections.",
    steps: "1. Multiple links can provide alternative paths if a connection fails. 2. Alternative paths can improve resilience when supported by the network design. 3. A full mesh requires n(n − 1) ÷ 2 links for n devices. 4. These links increase cabling, interface and maintenance costs.",
    ans: "Mesh topology can provide alternative paths that improve resilience, but a full mesh may be too expensive because the number of links grows rapidly as devices are added.",
    why: "Its reliability benefits must be weighed against connection and maintenance costs."
